<%= @instance.domain %> has added signals=on to its DNS record for <%= @host %>,
asking to take part in cross-instance signals.

Nothing changes until you approve it: its moderators see no matches, and its
applicants are not matched against other instances.

Before approving, make sure you know who runs <%= @instance.domain %>. The terms'
part on cross-instance signals explains why: the admin of a participating instance could probe
whether a given email address or network belongs to another participating
instance's applicants or members.

To approve:

  bin/rails "waterhole:herd:signals[<%= @instance.domain %>,approve]"

or, with Docker Compose:

  docker compose exec web bin/rails "waterhole:herd:signals[<%= @instance.domain %>,approve]"

To see every instance and what it is waiting for:

  bin/rails waterhole:herd:signals

The record as we read it:

  <%= @instance.verification_detail %>

--
Sent by the Waterhole at <%= @host %> because WATERHOLE_OPERATOR_EMAIL names you.
